  <h2>An industrial gateway OPC server with drivers for the equipment you already own</h2>
  <p>The Gateway speaks OPC UA, Modbus TCP and RTU, MQTT and Sparkplug B, EtherNet/IP, S7comm, MTConnect, HTTP, CODESYS, BACnet/IP, SNMP, UniFi Network, and OPC UA PubSub. The list is read from the drivers compiled into the binary, so a protocol cannot be advertised that is not there. Each protocol has moved real values off a real server or device and has been run on bare metal.</p>
  <p>The CODESYS driver reads and writes, and read a program of over 100,000 variables in 2.4 seconds. <a href="/integrations/">See every driver and what it was proven against</a>.</p>

  <h2>OPC UA in, OPC UA out</h2>
  <p>HotLoop Edge and the Gateway run an OPC UA server, so your SCADA reads what the Gateway collects from the Modbus, S7, and EtherNet/IP devices that never spoke OPC UA. It is the same job an OPC server does, with the historian and the alarms in the same process.</p>

